# Source: Slides "ICT3112 - 7 - Recepy for Loop Invariants - exercises", Exercise 4, and "tips a".
id: array-sum
title: Sum of an array
topic: Arrays
level: 3
source: Slides 7, Recipe exercises, Exercise 4
tags: arrays, loop, invariant, sum, definedness

task:
  Generalise the postcondition: $s$ is the sum of the first $i$ elements.
  What are the bounds? What is the variant? The loop reads $a[i]$, so the
  rule ARRAY-READ adds a definedness condition.

pre: n = sizeof(a)
post: s = sum(k, 0, n - 1, a[k])

program:
  {P}
  {R4}
  i := 0;              // i1
  {R3}
  s := 0;              // i2
  {I}
  while (i < n) do {
    {I && i < n}
    {R2}
    s := s + a[i];     // b1
    {R1}
    i := i + 1         // b2
    {I}
  }
  {I && !(i < n)}
  {Q}

verdict: valid

step: The invariant from a picture of the array
rule: WHILE-CONSEQUENCE
focus: while
text:
  The positions $0$ to $i - 1$ have been visited, and $s$ is their sum.
  The positions from $i$ to $n - 1$ have not been visited, and the loop
  only reads the array, so there is nothing to say about them. When
  $i = 0$ the sum is empty and its value is $0$. We also keep
  $n = sizeof(a)$, which the definedness condition will need.
set: I = s = sum(k, 0, i - 1, a[k]) && 0 <= i <= n && n = sizeof(a)

step: Establishment
rule: ASSIGN, SEQ, WP
focus: i1, i2
calc:
  wp(s := 0, I)
  = 0 = sum(k, 0, i - 1, a[k]) && 0 <= i <= n && n = sizeof(a)
set: R3 = 0 = sum(k, 0, i - 1, a[k]) && 0 <= i <= n && n = sizeof(a)
calc:
  wp(i := 0, R3)
  = 0 = sum(k, 0, 0 - 1, a[k]) && 0 <= 0 <= n && n = sizeof(a)
  = 0 <= n && n = sizeof(a)             // an empty sum is 0
set: R4 = 0 <= n && n = sizeof(a)
vc: n = sizeof(a) ==> 0 <= n && n = sizeof(a)
why:
  The size of an array is never negative.

step: Preservation
rule: ARRAY-READ, ASSIGN, SEQ, CONSEQUENCE
focus: b1, b2
calc:
  wp(i := i + 1, I)
  = s = sum(k, 0, i + 1 - 1, a[k]) && 0 <= i + 1 <= n && n = sizeof(a)
set: R1 = s = sum(k, 0, i, a[k]) && 0 <= i + 1 <= n && n = sizeof(a)
text:
  The next statement reads $a[i]$, so ARRAY-READ adds $def(a[i])$.
calc:
  wp(s := s + a[i], R1)
  = s + a[i] = sum(k, 0, i, a[k]) && 0 <= i + 1 <= n && n = sizeof(a) && def(a[i])
set: R2 = s + a[i] = sum(k, 0, i, a[k]) && 0 <= i + 1 <= n && n = sizeof(a) && def(a[i])
vc: I && i < n ==> R2
why:
  $sum(k, 0, i, a[k]) = sum(k, 0, i - 1, a[k]) + a[i] = s + a[i]$. The
  bounds follow from $0 <= i < n$. The read is defined, since
  $0 <= i < n = sizeof(a)$.

step: The postcondition at the exit
rule: CONSEQUENCE, LOGIC
vc: I && !(i < n) ==> s = sum(k, 0, n - 1, a[k])
why:
  $i >= n$ and $i <= n$ give $i = n$.
result: The triple is valid. A variant for termination is $n - i$.
